// Generated from this template by CMake, because the path has to be absolute
// and is only known at configure time.
//
// The filter travels inside the executable. It is a separate DLL because
// DirectShow loads it into whichever program opened the camera rather than into
// CapView, but shipping it as a separate file made the two able to disagree --
// and they did: Windows keeps
// the file locked while the camera is in use anywhere on the machine, so
// replacing it quietly failed and a new executable ended up talking to an old
// source. Carrying it means the executable can always lay down a copy that
// matches itself.
101 RCDATA "@VCAM_DLL_ESCAPED@"
